        "Content": "This hidden gem is perfectly positioned for those who appreciate outdoor activities.\r\nJust a short distance from the property lies a trekking trail, which winds its way along\r\na stunning route overlooking the bays and stretching out towards the Atlantic Ocean.\r\nFrom this vantage point, it is possible to watch large vessels as they traverse the\r\nAtlantic, heading towards distant shores.\r\nThe property boasts a garden of award-worthy design, with an impressive array of\r\nshrubs that enhance its natural beauty. The current owner is undoubtedly a talented\r\nand gifted gardener, whose passion for horticulture is evident throughout the\r\ngrounds.\r\nUpon acquiring the property, the current owners embarked on a thoughtful and\r\nstylish internal refit. Their meticulous approach is evident throughout the home,\r\nreflecting a commitment to quality and tasteful design. Notably, the bathroom stands\r\nout as a luxurious addition, having been installed by the present owner. It features a\r\nwalk-in shower which is attractively tiled, and a pedestal hand basin, and WC. The\r\nbathroom is further enhanced by a tiled floor and a frosted window at the rear,\r\nproviding both privacy and natural light. The attention to detail and high standard of\r\nfinish make this refurbished space a highlight of the property.\r\nThe kitchen has been thoughtfully designed to offer both functionality and style. It\r\nfeatures a generous selection of base units and ample worktop space, providing\r\nplenty of room for culinary preparation and storage. Integrated within the kitchen is\r\nan oven and hob, complemented by a stainless-steel inset sink, ensuring practicality\r\nfor day-to-day use. The space benefits from abundant natural light, thanks to the\r\ndouble-glazed windows positioned along the side and rear aspects, creating a bright\r\nand inviting atmosphere throughout the day.\r\nThe lounge is a standout feature of the property, offering an abundance of natural\r\nlight that creates a warm and inviting atmosphere. Double glazed windows are\r\nthoughtfully positioned at both the front and side of the room, ensuring that sunlight\r\nstreams in throughout the day. The space is finished with a fitted carpet, which adds\r\na layer of comfort and elegance to the lounge, making it an ideal setting for\r\nrelaxation or entertaining guests.\r\nThe hallway is fitted with stairs that lead up to a traditional attic space. In this area,\r\nthere is a WC and a wash hand basin, offering convenient facilities. With the\r\nappropriate planning permissions, this attic space could potentially be incorporated\r\ninto the main house, providing additional living space to suit various needs.\r\nBedrooms\r\nBoth bedrooms are tastefully decorated, maintaining a bright and airy atmosphere\r\nthroughout. The thoughtful design ensures comfort and a welcoming environment for\r\nresidents and guests alike.\r\nUtilities and Services\r\nHeating is supplied via oil-fired central heating, ensuring warmth throughout the\r\nproperty. The house benefits from private water supply, a septic tank for wastewater\r\nmanagement, and broadband connectivity for modern communication needs.\r\n\r\nGeneral Disclaimer / Important Notice\r\nThese particulars are issued by Irish Rural Homes for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, all descriptions, measurements, floor plans, boundaries, photographs, services, planning information and other details are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact.\r\nInterested parties should satisfy themselves fully as to the condition, title, boundaries, planning status, services, fixtures, fittings and all other matters relating to the property prior to entering into any contract. The property, lands and any outbuildings are offered as seen, and no warranty is given by the vendor or selling agent in relation to their condition, suitability, use or future development potential.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access is permitted to the dwelling, lands or farm buildings. Please contact Irish Rural Homes using the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a suitable viewing time."
